If reflection is a symmetry, then $[\mathcal M,H]=0.$ Suppose $H\ket{m}=E_m\ket{m}.$ Applying $\mathcal M$ gives $\begin{aligned}H\mathcal M\ket{m}
&=\mathcal M H\ket{m}\\
&=E_m\mathcal M\ket{m}.\end{aligned}$ Since $\mathcal M\ket{m}$ is the state with angular momentum $-m\hbar$, $E_{-m}=E_m.$ Rotation symmetry conserves angular momentum; reflection symmetry relates the two opposite values. Together they require the pair to be degenerate.

